9. Degree inflation and ATS filtering

There is a subtle distinction here.

Claim 1: degree filters exist

Yes.

Many recruitment systems allow employers to define education requirements, and recruiters can search/filter candidates by education.

A candidate who does not meet an explicit requirement may therefore never reach the hiring manager.

Confidence: High.

Claim 2: “ATS automatically rejects everyone without a degree”

This is too simplistic.

ATS platforms vary enormously, and employers configure their own workflows.

There is no reliable Irish statistic showing that, say, 73% of Irish graduate jobs automatically reject non-graduates.

So I would not build a career decision around that claim.

Confidence: High.

What changes after 3–5 years?

This is much more important.

Imagine:

